Optional small additions (defer to Batch 12 if scope balloons):
- crm/contact-logs/page.tsx — global list across all customers with customerId
  filter + type filter (mirror of crm/quotations/page.tsx layout).

### Item 2: Quotation UI Phase 2 (T2, ~25-30K)
Completes the quotation lifecycle. Two small additive features:

Files to touch:
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/crm/quotations/[id]/page.tsx — add a
  "Convert to invoice" button when status=accepted. Routes to a new endpoint
  on crm router (quotationConvertToInvoice) which atomically creates Invoice +
  InvoiceLineItems from QuotationLineItems and flips status to "converted".
  OR defer this and just add a PDF preview link.
- apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/crm.ts — add quotationConvertToInvoice
  procedure (writeProcedure, accepted-only, atomic creation, sets
  Quotation.convertedToInvoiceId).
- apps/web/src/__tests__/crm.test.ts — extend with ~5 tests for the conversion.
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/crm/quotations/[id]/pdf/page.tsx — NEW
  PDF preview page using react-pdf (add @react-pdf/renderer dep). Renders a
  printable quotation document with header + customer + sections + markup
  columns + line items + totals + terms.

## Pre-flight checks before starting Batch 11
1. `pnpm typecheck` && `pnpm vitest run` — confirm 595/595 GREEN baseline.
2. `pnpm db:migrate` confirmation — Migration #2 contact_logs must be applied.
3. Re-read .claude/rules/memory-governance.md §1 — Tiered Decomposition Engine.
4. Verify @react-pdf/renderer is installable before scoping the PDF preview;
   it has known issues on Next 15 server bundle — may need dynamic import.

